() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Seventy participants with fibromyalgia were randomized to receive 10 weeks of) Tj
T*
(individualized cognitive-behavioral therapy combined with routine treatment \(n = 35\) or) Tj
T*
(routine treatment alone \(n = 34\). Fifty-seven participants completed the study protocol.) Tj
T*
(At endpoint, the cognitive-behavioral therapy group demonstrated significant improvements) Tj
T*
(across all measured domains compared to controls. Anxiety scores \(Hospital Anxiety and) Tj
T*
(Depression Scale-anxiety subscale\) declined from median 13 to 10 points in the) Tj
T*
(intervention group versus 13 to 12 in controls \(p = 0.008\). Depression scores similarly) Tj
T*
(improved \(13 to 9 versus 13 to 11, p = 0.006\). Jenkins Sleep Scale scores showed greater) Tj
T*
(benefit in the intervention arm \(p = 0.002\). Disease-specific functional impairment) Tj
T*
(\(Fibromyalgia Impact Questionnaire\) declined from median 64 to 48 in the cognitive-) Tj
T*
(behavioral therapy group compared to 63 to 58 in controls \(p = 0.003\). Beck Hopelessness) Tj
T*
(Scale scores decreased more substantially with combined intervention \(p = 0.009\). These) Tj
T*
(findings support integration of individualized psychological intervention into) Tj
T*
(fibromyalgia treatment pathways.) Tj
